# Smart Helmet Architecture & Classification Guide

## 1. Smart Helmet System Architecture

| Primary Sub-Domain | Core Purpose | Key Hardware Components | Typical Lightweight Stack |
| :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- |
| **Incident Management & Emergency Response** | Detects high-g impacts/falls and auto-transmits emergency GPS coordinates | MPU6050 IMU, NEO-6M GPS, SIM800L GSM, Microcontroller | ESP32-C3 / ESP32-S3 + MPU6050 + SIM7000G (LTE-M) |
| **Smart Ignition Interlock & Verification** | Prevents vehicle engine ignition unless helmet is worn and rider is sober | MQ-3 Alcohol Sensor, IR/FSR Presence Sensors, RF/Bluetooth Relay | Arduino Nano BLE Sense + Optical IR Sensor + BLE Module |
| **Environmental & Industrial Hazard Sensing** | Tracks ambient toxic gases, CO2, temperature, and humidity for workers | MQ-135 (CO2), MQ-7 (CO), DHT22, OLED display, Buzzer | ESP32 (Deep Sleep) + BME680 MEMS Sensor + LiPo Battery |
| **Augmented Rider Assistance & HUD** | Projects navigation arrows, speed limits, and warnings onto the visor | Micro OLED/TFT display, optical prism lens, Bluetooth module | Raspberry Pi Pico W / ESP32 + Mobile Map API App |
| **Fatigue & Drowsiness Alerting** | Tracks driver eye-blink patterns or head tilts to trigger haptic alerts | IR eye-blink sensor, strap vibration sensor, coin vibration motor | Raspberry Pi Pico W + Visor IR Sensor + Haptic Feedback |

