## 2. Physical Form Factor Classification & Structural Integration

| Helmet Type | Structural Coverage | Smart Tech Integration Suitability | Key Target Use Case |
| :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- |
| **Full-Face** | Complete head, chin, and face protection | **High**: Ideal space for HUD displays, internal audio, and integrated rear cameras. | High-speed riding & full-feature smart prototypes |
| **Modular / Flip-Up** | Hinged chin bar flips upward | **Medium**: Requires flexible wire routing across chin hinge joints. | Touring riders & urban commuting |
| **Open-Face (3/4) & Half** | Covers top/sides or top only | **Low**: Limited housing space; relies on external clip-on Bluetooth modules. | Short-distance urban travel |
| **Dual-Sport / ADV** | Full-face with off-road visor/peak | **Medium**: Suitable for rugged sensor placement and off-road GPS tracking. | Off-road & adventure touring |
| **Industrial Safety** | Hard-hat form factor | **High**: High room for top-mounted gas sensors, fall sensors, and mesh radio. | Construction sites, mining, & factory worker safety |

